{
 "title": "Statehood",
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Statehood",
   "card": false,
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "c108",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "The Creek Nation was splitting in two.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c109",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "One side wanted to live alongside the Americans.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c110",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "The other side, called the Red Sticks, wanted",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c111",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "the settlers out.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c112",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "It became a civil war inside the Creek",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c113",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Nation.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c114",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "And then it dragged in the United States.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c115",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "August 1813.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c116",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Red Stick warriors attack Fort Mims, north of",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c117",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Mobile.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c118",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Hundreds of people inside are killed.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c119",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "March 1814.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c120",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "At a bend in the Tallapoosa River called",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c121",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Horseshoe Bend, an American general named Andrew Jackson",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c122",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "attacks the Red Sticks with soldiers, militia, and",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c123",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Cherokee and Creek allies.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c124",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "More than 800 Red Stick warriors die in",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c125",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "a single day.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c126",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Then Jackson made all the Creeks sign the",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c127",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "peace treaty, even the ones who had fought",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c128",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "on his side.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c129",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "The Creek Nation handed over 23 million acres,",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c130",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "much of what is now Alabama.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c131",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "23 million acres of empty map.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c132",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "And America went wild.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c133",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "They called it Alabama Fever.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c134",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Farmers sold everything they owned in Georgia, the",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c135",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Carolinas, and Tennessee and rushed west for cheap",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c136",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "land and one crop, cotton.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c137",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "In 1810, the census counted fewer than 10,000",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c138",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "people here.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c139",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Ten years later, more than 125,000.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c140",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "December 14, 1819.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c141",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Alabama becomes the 22nd state.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c142",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Then it needed a capital.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c143",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "This took a while.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c144",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "The first permanent one was a river town",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c145",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "called Cahawba.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c146",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "It kept flooding.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c147",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "So they moved to Tuscaloosa.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c148",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Then they moved again.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c149",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Alabama had five different capitals in under 30",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c150",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "years.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c151",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "The last one was a cotton town on",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c152",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "a bluff over the Alabama River.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c153",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Montgomery.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c154",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "And in 1846, Alabama built its Capitol on",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c155",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "a hill at the top of Montgomery's main",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c156",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "street.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c157",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "The street ran straight down the hill to",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c158",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "a fountain in a square.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c159",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Five blocks.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c160",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Remember this street.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c161",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "The story of Alabama is going to keep",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c162",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "walking down it.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c163",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Oh, and around this time, a newspaper announced",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c164",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "that the word Alabama meant here we rest.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c165",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "It sounded beautiful and it stuck for generations.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c166",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Experts in the actual language, they never found",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c167",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "any word like it.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c168",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "And the native nations who had lived here",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c169",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "for 10,000 years, they were not allowed",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c170",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "to rest anywhere.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c171",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "In the 1830s, the government forced the Creek,",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c172",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "the Cherokee, the Choctaw, and the Chickasaw to",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c173",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "leave.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c174",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Tens of thousands of people were marched west.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c175",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Thousands died on the way.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c176",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "A few families stayed and held on.",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c177",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Their descendants are the Poarch Band of Creek",
     "date": null
    },
    {
     "id": "c178",
     "shot": "todo_statehood",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Indians, and they are still in Alabama today.",
     "date": null
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}